      "api_analysis": {
        "hypothesis": "The existing custom_ops.cu exports launchers with raw pointers and cudaStream_t. The missing binding file must wrap these launchers in torch::Tensor functions and register them via TORCH_LIBRARY to expose torch.ops.cuda_extension.*. The error 'incompatible with the pybind module' occurs because model_new.py calls torch.ops.cuda_extension.*, but the extension only registers pybind functions. Adding a TORCH_LIBRARY block in a kernels/*_binding.cpp file will resolve registration, and correct tensor handling will ensure numerical correctness.",
        "evidence": [
          "model_new.py calls torch.ops.cuda_extension.conv_transpose_forward, clamp_forward, leaky_relu_forward, triu_forward, add_forward.",
          "binding_registry.h only supports pybind module registration, not torch.ops registration.",
          "custom_ops.cu defines launchers but does not include torch/library.h or register operators.",
          "No existing binding file in kernels/ means these torch.ops symbols are missing, causing the reported errors."
        ],
        "changes": [
